  "body": "What happens: the `detect_holes` row in `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` says that a Bore operation skips each hole wider than `d + 4 * reach + 2 * stock_to_leave`. PR #1839 (#1566) removed that limit. Bore now clears a wide hole with concentric rings.\n\nExpected: the row states the current law in `crates/app/src/operation/bore_reach.rs` and `crates/motion/src/machining2d/bore_core.rs`:\n- A hole is skipped when the ring plan needs more than 4096 rings.\n- A hole is skipped when the floor band of the tool is zero. An example is a ball cutter at a flat blind floor.\n- If each detected hole is skipped, the tool refuses with `no hole this Bore op can make: ...` and stores nothing.\n\nEvidence: found while fixing #1909. The two UI tests of `crates/ui/src/detect_holes_note_tests.rs` failed on main for the same cause.\n\nNote: the file is a process file. The PR body needs the line `Process change: yes`.\n\nDone means: the skill row matches the current Bore rule, and a docs-only PR merges.\n",
